<%# A capability, shown rather than described: one genuine screenshot of the running product beside the two
  or three things that screen actually does.

  WHY THIS IS NOT `walkthrough`. A walkthrough's picture carries numbered markers and its items ARE those
  markers, so the two must agree or the figure lies. A showcase's picture carries no markers, its items are
  the capability's own points, and its job is to put the reader inside the screen they would be working in.
  Serving both from one type meant either numbering points that nothing on the image pointed at, or shipping
  a figure with no explanation beside it -- which is how the home page ended up with nine identical text
  cards and no product in sight.

  ALTERNATING, AND THAT IS THE POINT. `media_position` is `start` or `end`, and consecutive showcases down a
  page alternate, so the eye crosses the measure instead of running down one rail of identical slabs. The
  DOM order is always picture-then-text whichever side the picture is drawn on, so the order a screen reader
  and a keyboard follow never depends on the decoration.

  THE SCREENSHOT IS A REAL CAPTURE OR THE SECTION DOES NOT RENDER. There is no placeholder and no drawn
  mock-up: `page.image_for` returns nil for a missing attachment and the figure is simply absent, which
  leaves an honest text block rather than a fabricated dashboard. The hero's old hand-built "Shared inbox"
  panel is exactly what this rule exists to prevent.

  WIDTH AND HEIGHT COME FROM THE BLOB, for the reason _image.html.erb gives: a screenshot is the largest
  thing in the band and a missing intrinsic size is the one that shifts the layout under the reader as it
  lands. Emitted only when the blob was analysed, because a guess would be worse than none.
%>
<% attachment = page&.image_for(section['attachment_id']) %>
<% points = Array(section['items']) %>
<% media_end = section['media_position'].to_s == 'end' %>

<section class="<%= tone %>">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
      <% if attachment.present? %>
        <figure class="<%= 'lg:order-last' if media_end %>">
          <%# The plate under the screenshot: a soft indigo wash and a ring, so a light screenshot on a light
              band still reads as a separate object rather than bleeding into the page. %>
          <div class="relative rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-lyn-indigo/10 via-lyn-blue/5 to-transparent p-2 sm:p-3">
            <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-lyn-line shadow-[0_24px_60px_-24px_rgba(10,23,51,0.45)]">
              <img src="<%= marketing_media_path(id: attachment.id) %>"
                   alt="<%= section['alt'].to_s %>"
                   <%= "width=#{attachment.blob.metadata['width']} height=#{attachment.blob.metadata['height']}".html_safe if attachment.blob.metadata['width'].present? %>
                   loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   class="block w-full">
            </div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      <% end %>

      <div class="<%= 'lg:order-first' if media_end %>">
        <% if section['kicker'].present? %>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-lyn-indigo"><%= section['kicker'] %></p>
        <% end %>
        <% if section['heading'].present? %>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-lyn-ink sm:text-4xl">
            <%= section['heading'] %>
          </h2>
        <% end %>
        <% if section['lede'].present? %>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink-soft"><%= section['lede'] %></p>
        <% end %>

        <% if points.any? %>
          <ul class="mt-8 space-y-5">
            <% points.each do |point| %>
              <li class="flex gap-3.5">
                <%# `aria-hidden` on the tick: it is punctuation for the eye, and a screen reader announcing
                    "check mark" before every item in a list it already knows is a list is noise. %>
                <span aria-hidden="true"
                      class="mt-0.5 grid size-6 flex-none place-content-center rounded-full bg-lyn-indigo/10 text-lyn-indigo">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="size-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"
                       stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><path d="m3.5 8.5 3 3 6-7"/></svg>
                </span>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <% if point['title'].present? %>
                    <p class="text-base font-semibold text-lyn-ink"><%= point['title'] %></p>
                  <% end %>
                  <% if point['body'].present? %>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-base leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink-soft"><%= point['body'] %></p>
                  <% end %>
                </div>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
        <% end %>

        <% if section['link_label'].present? && section['link_target'].present? %>
          <% href = marketing_target_href(section['link_target']) %>
          <% if href %>
            <a href="<%= href %>"
               class="mt-8 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-1.5 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-royal transition-colors hover:text-lyn-indigo-deep focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
              <%= section['link_label'] %>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="rtl:-scale-x-100">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
